# 4. Conventions & Policies

## Commit Discipline

Commit files as you create or meaningfully edit them — don't let uncommitted work accumulate. After completing a logical unit of work (new file, feature, fix, refactor), stage and commit immediately before moving on to the next task. Batching commits at the end of a session leads to forgotten files, muddled history, and stranded work if the session ends unexpectedly.

## Cross-Repo Workflows

For interconnected Go repositories:

```bash
# After pushing dependency changes
cd /path/to/dependent
go get <module>@latest && go mod tidy && go build ./...
```

| Dependency | Dependent | Integration |
|------------|-----------|-------------|
| Intermute | Autarch | Embedded server, domain API |

Common issues: 404 → dependency not pushed; build errors → run `go get <dep>@latest`

## Credential Safety

**NEVER include API tokens, secrets, or credentials in public GitHub issues, PRs, comments, or documentation.** Always redact to `ntn_xxx...` or similar placeholders. If a token is accidentally exposed, flag it immediately so the user can rotate it.

## Destructive Command Guard (dcg)

PreToolUse hook that blocks destructive Bash commands before execution. Matters most on zklw, where agents run with `--dangerously-skip-permissions`.

- **Binary**: `~/.local/bin/dcg` (v0.4.0, x86_64-linux-gnu) — zklw only
- **Config**: `~/.config/dcg/config.toml` (self-heal disabled)
- **Source**: https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/destructive_command_guard

**What it blocks** (core packs, on by default):
- `core.git`: `git reset --hard`, `git push --force`, `git clean -f`, `git branch -D`, `git stash drop/clear`, `git checkout --`
- `core.filesystem`: `rm -rf` outside `/tmp`/`$TMPDIR`

**Behavior**: Fail-open — if dcg crashes or times out (200ms deadline), the command is allowed. `DCG_BYPASS=1` disables all protection (escape hatch). Self-heal is disabled, so dcg will NOT re-inject its own hook into settings.json.

**If dcg blocks a needed command**: Ask the user to run it manually. Do not attempt to bypass dcg.

> **Wiring status, re-verified 2026-08-03 — read this before relying on the above.**
> **`dcg` itself is still installed and registered nowhere.** The binary
